{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KQBBj9ZUqZhDR9UWuAt7yQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: prd013-true\n     2→title: \"cmd/true: Exit Successfully\"\n     3→\n     4→problem: |\n     5→  Shell scripts use true as a no-op command that always succeeds. It appears in conditional\n     6→  expressions, while loops (while true; do ...; done), and as a placeholder in pipelines.\n     7→  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtrue, installed by\n     8→  coreutils) in exit code behavior, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n     9→\n    10→goals:\n    11→  - G1: Exit with status 0 unconditionally, ignoring all arguments.\n    12→  - G2: Produce no output unless --help or --version is given.\n    13→\n    14→requirements:\n    15→  R1:\n    16→    title: Core behavior\n    17→    items:\n    18→      - R1.1: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with no arguments.\n    19→      - R1.2: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with any arguments, ignoring them entirely. Arguments are not parsed, validated, or acted upon.\n    20→      - R1.3: Must not read from stdin. Must not write to stdout or stderr under normal operation (no arguments or unrecognized arguments).\n    21→\n    22→  R2:\n    23→    title: Help and version output\n    24→    items:\n    25→      - R2.1: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0.\n    26→      - R2.2: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0.\n    27→      - R2.3: If a write error occurs while printing --help or --version output, must exit 1.\n    28→\n    29→  R3:\n    30→    title: Exit codes\n    31→    items:\n    32→      - R3.1: Must exit 0 in all cases except a write error during --help or --version output.\n    33→      - R3.2: Must not exit with any status other than 0 or 1.\n    34→\n    35→  R4:\n    36→    title: Differential testing\n    37→    items:\n    38→      - R4.1: Differential tests must compare exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\n    39→      - R4.2: \"Tests must cover: no arguments, arbitrary arguments (ignored), --help output, and --version output.\"\n    40→      - R4.3: Tests must verify that no output is produced on stdout or stderr when invoked without --help or --version.\n    41→\n    42→non_goals:\n    43→  - cmd/true does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version.\n    44→  - cmd/true does not perform any computation or I/O beyond the optional help/version output.\n    45→\n    46→acceptance_criteria:\n    47→  - \"AC1: go run ./cmd/true; echo $? prints 0.\"\n    48→  - \"AC2: go run ./cmd/true foo bar --baz; echo $? prints 0.\"\n    49→  - \"AC3: go run ./cmd/true --help prints a usage message and exits 0, matching gtrue --help.\"\n    50→  - \"AC4: Differential test against gtrue passes for no-args and arbitrary-args cases.\"\n    51→  - \"AC5: cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    52→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea57d0f1-7494-40c3-b9dd-04669af0d596","uuid":"95cc1568-13c8-4158-b26f-51344f33dc05","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/331/docs/specs/product-requirements/prd013-true.yaml","content":"id: prd013-true\ntitle: \"cmd/true: Exit Successfully\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts use true as a no-op command that always succeeds. It appears in conditional\n  expressions, while loops (while true; do ...; done), and as a placeholder in pipelines.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtrue, installed by\n  coreutils) in exit code behavior, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Exit with status 0 unconditionally, ignoring all arguments.\n  - G2: Produce no output unless --help or --version is given.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Core behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with no arguments.\n      - R1.2: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with any arguments, ignoring them entirely. Arguments are not parsed, validated, or acted upon.\n      - R1.3: Must not read from stdin. Must not write to stdout or stderr under normal operation (no arguments or unrecognized arguments).\n\n  R2:\n    title: Help and version output\n    items:\n      - R2.1: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0.\n      - R2.2: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0.\n      - R2.3: If a write error occurs while printing --help or --version output, must exit 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes\n    items:\n      - R3.1: Must exit 0 in all cases except a write error during --help or --version output.\n      - R3.2: Must not exit with any status other than 0 or 1.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1: Differential tests must compare exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2: \"Tests must cover: no arguments, arbitrary arguments (ignored), --help output, and --version output.\"\n      - R4.3: Tests must verify that no output is produced on stdout or stderr when invoked without --help or --version.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/true does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version.\n  - cmd/true does not perform any computation or I/O beyond the optional help/version output.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: go run ./cmd/true; echo $? prints 0.\"\n  - \"AC2: go run ./cmd/true foo bar --baz; echo $? prints 0.\"\n  - \"AC3: go run ./cmd/true --help prints a usage message and exits 0, matching gtrue --help.\"\n  - \"AC4: Differential test against gtrue passes for no-args and arbitrary-args cases.\"\n  - \"AC5: cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}}}
