e same arguments and environment.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The harness compares exit codes. Both binaries must exit 1 for normal invocations.\n      No stdout or stderr comparison is needed for the default case.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/false — unconditional exit 1, argument ignoring (prd014-false R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, exit code comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/false compiles and ./bin/false exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: ./bin/false exits with status 1 when invoked with no arguments.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: ./bin/false exits with status 1 when invoked with arbitrary arguments.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test passes for no-args and arbitrary-args cases, confirming\n      exit code parity with gfalse.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - --help and --version output formatting is verified manually, not via differential testing.\n  - Write-error exit code (R2.3) is not tested in the differential harness.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel02.0\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1,"totalLines":55}}}
