ctory is set correctly when calling `go build` from the test, since the test runs in the package directory.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the constraints about not reading files in the repository and implementing from the provided specifications instead. I should finalize my implementation plan and write out all the necessary files, keeping in mind Go 1.26 compatibility.\n\nI need to be careful about how `go build` handles working directories during tests—when running `go test ./cmd/true/`, the working directory is already `cmd/true/`, so the build command needs to account for that. The module path is `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`, so my imports will reference `pkg/sys` and `pkg/testutils` from that module path.\n\nReady to write the implementation now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":498,"cache_read_input_tokens":47775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":498},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea57d0f1-7494-40c3-b9dd-04669af0d596","uuid":"11e63012-0a7e-4bfc-987b-0a44d8f6a4ba"}
